<BaseLayout title="Qualia · Nizam Mohammed" description="Qualia, a world model of musical experience learned from how people listen rather than from audio. Published on arXiv, with a conference paper in progress." headerVariant="internal" activeNav="work">
<article class="project"><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--top">← Work</a><header class="project__hero"><div class="project__hero-media project__hero-media--shot"><a class="pshot pshot--link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.10862" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the Project Qualia paper on arXiv"><img src="/project/qualia-card.jpg" alt="The Project Qualia paper on arXiv"><span class="pshot__cue">View on arXiv</span></a></div><div class="project__hero-heading"><h1 class="project__title page-heading-reveal">Qualia</h1><p class="project__hero-sub">A world model of musical experience, learned from listening behavior rather than audio.</p><div class="project__hero-actions"><a class="project__hero-cta" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.10862" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the paper</a><span class="project__hero-id">arXiv:2609.10862</span></div></div></header><div class="project__meta project__meta--role"><span class="project__status"><span class="project__status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>In Progress</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Research project</span></div><p class="project__role"><span class="project__role-label">Role</span>Lead researcher</p><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">About</p><div class="project__body"><p>Qualia is a research project developing a world model of musical experience, learned from listening behavior rather than from audio. It is being built in stages, and the first stage is now published.</p></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">The paper</p><div class="project__body"><div class="paper-card"><p class="paper-card__eyebrow">Published · arXiv, 2026</p><h2 class="paper-card__title">Project Qualia: Recovering Experiential Music Structure from Session Co-occurrence Data</h2><p class="paper-card__authors">Nizam Mohammed, with Abu B. S. Rahman and Dimuthu D. K. Arachchige (Hampton University)</p><p class="paper-card__id">arXiv:2609.10862</p><p class="paper-card__desc">It introduces a custom behavioral corpus of 531.6 million training scrobbles across 28.6 million listening sessions, and reports the first result: trained on session co-occurrence alone, with no genre labels and no audio, the embedding space is dominated by artist identity, and after that identity is removed, structure beyond it remains.</p><a class="paper-card__btn" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.10862" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the paper</a></div></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">What it shows</p><div class="project__body"><p>After subtracting each artist's average from its tracks, most cross-artist similarity drops to near zero, as expected. A small number of pairs remain close, and these tend to be genre- and era-coherent. Artist identity is reduced, not removed.</p><figure class="chart"><svg class="qc-two" viewBox="0 0 720 232" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Two distributions of residual cosine on one axis: random cross-artist pairs near zero and never past 0.70, and each track's nearest cross-artist neighbor centered near 0.45 with a tail that crosses 0.70, about 8 standard deviations beyond chance."><style>.qc-two text{font-family:var(--font-sans,"Inter",system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif);fill:var(--stone,#7A7268);font-size:10.5px}.qc-two .num{font-family:var(--font-mono,ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace)}.qc-two .ember{fill:var(--ember,#A0521C)}.qc-two .nbar{fill:var(--stone,#7A7268);opacity:.34}.qc-two .dbar{fill:var(--ember,#A0521C);opacity:.42}.qc-two .base{stroke:var(--hairline,#E8E2D8)}.qc-two .thr{stroke:var(--ember,#A0521C);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:3 3}.qc-two .sw-n{fill:var(--stone,#7A7268);opacity:.6}.qc-two .sw-d{fill:var(--ember,#A0521C);opacity:.75}</style><rect class="nbar" x="13.0" y="195.9" width="4.6" height="0.1"/><rect class="nbar" x="23.1" y="195.9" width="